    "doi": null,
    "title_en": "Evidence for the decay $B^0 \\to μ^+ μ^-$ and improved measurements of the decay $B^0_s \\to μ^+ μ^-$",
    "abstract_en": "The first single-experiment evidence for the rare decay $B^0 \\to μ^+ μ^-$ and the world's most precise measurements of the $B^0_s \\to μ^+ μ^-$ branching fraction and effective lifetime are reported. The results are obtained using Run 3 proton-proton collision data corresponding to an integrated luminosity of 18 fb$^{-1}$ recorded with the LHCb Upgrade I detector at a centre-of-mass energy of $13.6$ TeV between 2024 and 2025. Their combination with the Run 1 and Run 2 LHCb results further improves the precision. All measurements are found to be in agreement with the Standard Model expectations.",
